1
00:00:04,738 --> 00:00:08,441
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

2
00:00:17,117 --> 00:00:19,552
5TH CYBER MATCH

3
00:00:24,657 --> 00:00:28,862
A Shogi, or Japanese chess, match
between a human and a robot.

4
00:00:30,764 --> 00:00:35,869
Shogi prodigy Goro Gotanda
whose winning streak remains unbroken

5
00:00:36,002 --> 00:00:39,406
versus Mongoose,
the world's strongest Shogi robot.

6
00:00:39,739 --> 00:00:41,107
The fifth Cyber Match.

7
00:00:41,307 --> 00:00:45,412
Gotanda is being forced into
an extremely inferior position.

8
00:00:45,612 --> 00:00:49,182
Does he have a miraculous
comeback move?

9
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,659
SCORE

10
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,796
You suck. Try again.

11
00:01:04,531 --> 00:01:06,166
The machine's strong.

12
00:01:10,136 --> 00:01:13,773
Dr. Inomata's occult
tumor surgery created

13
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:17,210
a huge impact on
the medical community.

14
00:01:17,343 --> 00:01:20,914
Every day, he's inundated with
requests from universities

15
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:22,715
to give a lecture.

16
00:01:23,216 --> 00:01:26,586
Today, he's at Sapporo
Medical and Dental University.

17
00:01:26,653 --> 00:01:28,221
That's wonderful.

18
00:01:28,288 --> 00:01:32,292
Totei must be on the front line
of universities in Japan.

19
00:01:32,826 --> 00:01:34,494
Yes sir…I mean, yes.

20
00:01:35,929 --> 00:01:40,900
Speaking of front line, have you
heard of an AI called Hippocrates?

21
00:01:40,967 --> 00:01:44,671
Of course. It's already been
implemented in our hospital.

22
00:01:45,038 --> 00:01:46,372
Hippocrates.

23
00:01:46,639 --> 00:01:51,144
AI fed with over 50 million
pieces of medical literature

24
00:01:51,211 --> 00:01:54,180
instantly identifies the disease
based on a patient's data

25
00:01:54,247 --> 00:01:57,684
and determines the most
appropriate treatment.

26
00:01:57,851 --> 00:02:00,987
A cutting-edge medical AI.

27
00:02:01,321 --> 00:02:05,892
It was named after Hippocrates,
the father of medicine.

28
00:02:06,092 --> 00:02:08,094
I want you to

29
00:02:09,295 --> 00:02:11,965
whip up a splendid case
using Hippocrates.

30
00:02:14,868 --> 00:02:15,702
Splendid?

31
00:02:19,072 --> 00:02:20,773
This? Are you curious?

32
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:22,742
Very curious.

33
00:02:22,909 --> 00:02:26,079
I'm featured as the leader of medicine.

34
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:27,981
A publisher talked me into it.

35
00:02:28,114 --> 00:02:29,749
May I take a look?

36
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:31,184
Sure...

37
00:02:31,518 --> 00:02:33,153
Thank you.

38
00:02:33,653 --> 00:02:35,088
<i>In 2017</i>

39
00:02:35,688 --> 00:02:40,560
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

40
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:48,001
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

41
00:02:50,236 --> 00:02:53,139
After Totei's success with
artificial intelligence

42
00:02:53,773 --> 00:02:57,744
other universities will
follow your example.

43
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:01,748
Many patients will be saved by AI.

44
00:03:01,881 --> 00:03:05,051
In which case,
the Japan Doctors Club

45
00:03:05,385 --> 00:03:09,355
will gain many benefits.
Isn't that right?

46
00:03:09,822 --> 00:03:10,957
No.

47
00:03:12,992 --> 00:03:15,295
I said nothing of the sort.

48
00:03:22,902 --> 00:03:25,405
MEDICINE IS LOVE

49
00:03:25,672 --> 00:03:27,574
All I'm saying is

50
00:03:28,942 --> 00:03:30,677
I want a good steak.

51
00:03:33,379 --> 00:03:35,815
I read between the lines.

52
00:03:46,859 --> 00:03:49,596
I'm counting on you, gentlemen.

53
00:03:51,164 --> 00:03:51,998
Yes sir.

54
00:03:58,805 --> 00:04:02,275
Please let me do a splendid
case using Hippocrates.

55
00:04:02,842 --> 00:04:04,477
Dr. Torii?

56
00:04:05,878 --> 00:04:08,581
I'm skeptical of AI.

57
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:12,085
It's artificial after all.
Produced by man.

58
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:16,089
I can't imagine how it can
surpass human intelligence.

59
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:17,957
You say it with certainty.

60
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:23,363
It's our duty to present a diagnosis
carefully and diligently.

61
00:04:23,663 --> 00:04:27,500
We owe it to the patients
who entrust their lives to us.

62
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:29,535
How admirable of you.

63
00:04:30,136 --> 00:04:31,237
Thank you.

64
00:04:32,972 --> 00:04:34,140
But Dr. Torii...

65
00:04:35,041 --> 00:04:38,678
keep talking like that
and you'll lose your job.

66
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:42,782
It may take you 10 years
to complete a research.

67
00:04:44,384 --> 00:04:45,418
AI can do it

68
00:04:47,387 --> 00:04:48,354
in one second.

69
00:04:51,858 --> 00:04:52,725
One second.

70
00:04:55,795 --> 00:05:00,600
SWEET WAFFLES

71
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,235
- I'll take one.
- Yes, ma'am.

72
00:05:08,107 --> 00:05:09,208
No discount.

73
00:05:10,176 --> 00:05:11,377
Sorry.

74
00:05:12,111 --> 00:05:16,749
<i>In the midst of this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

75
00:05:16,949 --> 00:05:21,054
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

76
00:05:22,789 --> 00:05:26,459
I lost. I'm hungry.

77
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:29,629
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

78
00:05:30,296 --> 00:05:34,100
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

79
00:05:34,967 --> 00:05:40,173
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

80
00:05:41,808 --> 00:05:43,810
CYBER MATCH

81
00:05:45,878 --> 00:05:46,979
What?

82
00:05:47,613 --> 00:05:49,382
It's not over yet?

83
00:05:50,416 --> 00:05:52,218
He's still thinking?

84
00:05:52,652 --> 00:05:54,220
As he should be.

85
00:05:54,287 --> 00:05:57,590
His next move could change
the history of Shogi.

86
00:05:58,191 --> 00:06:01,494
I didn't know you were
such a Shogi fan.

87
00:06:01,694 --> 00:06:05,698
Former captain of the Shogi club
at her middle and high schools.

88
00:06:05,832 --> 00:06:06,799
Really?

89
00:06:08,501 --> 00:06:09,335
There he goes.

90
00:06:09,836 --> 00:06:12,739
His Knight from Hell maneuver?

91
00:06:12,872 --> 00:06:13,706
KNIGHT

92
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:16,175
Thank you very much.

93
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:31,958
What is he doing?

94
00:06:32,225 --> 00:06:33,393
What's happening?

95
00:06:33,459 --> 00:06:34,861
I think he's in trouble.

96
00:06:42,168 --> 00:06:43,469
Mr. Gotanda!

97
00:06:43,703 --> 00:06:45,338
Call an ambulance!

98
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:46,639
Hurry!

99
00:06:50,176 --> 00:06:52,345
That tremor...
Possible brain hemorrhage.

100
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:53,813
Or a brain tumor.

101
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:56,416
Maybe hypoglycemia.

102
00:06:57,450 --> 00:06:59,752
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

103
00:07:00,353 --> 00:07:01,387
<i>Also known as...</i>

104
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:03,556
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

105
00:07:32,552 --> 00:07:34,220
AI can't be trusted.

106
00:07:35,421 --> 00:07:36,923
Humans make diagnoses.

107
00:07:40,893 --> 00:07:42,795
- Treatment room.
- Yes, doctor.

108
00:07:44,197 --> 00:07:45,498
Mr. Gotanda!

109
00:07:45,731 --> 00:07:47,133
Can you hear us?!

110
00:07:57,410 --> 00:07:59,212
Can you hear me?

111
00:08:03,749 --> 00:08:05,384
I'm Deputy Chief Surgeon Torii.

112
00:08:05,685 --> 00:08:06,519
His condition?

113
00:08:07,119 --> 00:08:10,156
Spasm was relieved by diazepam.
Level 1 consciousness.

114
00:08:10,223 --> 00:08:11,691
Get a brain MRI.

115
00:08:12,658 --> 00:08:14,827
We'll get you tested right away.

116
00:08:31,077 --> 00:08:32,078
Worked all night?

117
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,315
- Good morning.
- Don't get up.

118
00:08:43,422 --> 00:08:44,257
Good morning.

119
00:08:49,495 --> 00:08:51,230
Mr. Gotanda's MRI?

120
00:08:52,298 --> 00:08:53,733
Were you up all night?

121
00:08:53,966 --> 00:08:55,868
They must be brain tumors.

122
00:08:57,169 --> 00:08:59,739
This image doesn't confirm it.

123
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:02,575
I know.

124
00:09:04,277 --> 00:09:07,380
Harvard Medical School
used AI to diagnose

125
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:12,118
a case that baffled its doctors
for half a year.

126
00:09:12,818 --> 00:09:13,786
AI?

127
00:09:13,853 --> 00:09:16,422
Why don't you run it
through Hippocrates?

128
00:09:18,558 --> 00:09:23,963
An accurate diagnosis is made by
a doctor with years of experience.

129
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:25,898
Of course, sir.

130
00:09:34,707 --> 00:09:36,042
You've stabilized.

131
00:09:36,842 --> 00:09:38,244
How are you feeling?

132
00:09:38,811 --> 00:09:40,012
Absolutely fine.

133
00:09:42,381 --> 00:09:45,151
Your test results...

134
00:09:46,485 --> 00:09:47,653
What's wrong with me?

135
00:09:48,688 --> 00:09:49,722
Well...

136
00:09:52,959 --> 00:09:55,494
A serious disease?

137
00:09:55,928 --> 00:09:57,496
Oh, no...

138
00:10:03,836 --> 00:10:05,938
Then what? Tell me.

139
00:10:07,073 --> 00:10:07,907
Um...

140
00:10:11,110 --> 00:10:12,645
Hippocrates has the answer.

141
00:10:13,346 --> 00:10:14,614
Hippocrates?

142
00:10:14,747 --> 00:10:16,215
Cutting-edge AI.

143
00:10:18,751 --> 00:10:19,652
AI...

144
00:10:20,186 --> 00:10:21,120
Yes.

145
00:10:24,223 --> 00:10:25,992
That won't be necessary.

146
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:27,893
I have another
match.

147
00:10:28,527 --> 00:10:29,528
I'm leaving.

148
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:40,706
Wait a minute.

149
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:43,776
You lost to a machine.

150
00:10:43,909 --> 00:10:44,777
Daimon...

151
00:10:45,011 --> 00:10:46,045
Let me see.

152
00:10:46,512 --> 00:10:47,647
Open and close.

153
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:50,650
Does it hurt?

154
00:10:51,784 --> 00:10:52,618
Not really.

155
00:10:53,219 --> 00:10:55,821
Ever had a hand spasm
and collapsed before yesterday?

156
00:10:56,589 --> 00:10:57,990
Who are you?

157
00:10:58,057 --> 00:10:59,158
A freelance surgeon.

158
00:10:59,358 --> 00:11:00,226
Freelance?

159
00:11:00,459 --> 00:11:03,129
- A part-timer. Stay out of this.
- Why?

160
00:11:03,262 --> 00:11:04,263
Excuse me.

161
00:11:04,397 --> 00:11:06,032
Please wait.

162
00:11:06,098 --> 00:11:06,932
Hey.

163
00:11:07,366 --> 00:11:08,834
Mr. Gotanda...

164
00:11:13,606 --> 00:11:15,875
Isn't that Mr. Gotanda?

165
00:11:18,310 --> 00:11:21,347
Mr. Gotanda!
Are you feeling better?

166
00:11:21,614 --> 00:11:25,518
Is it true you feigned illness
because you were losing?

167
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,420
Tell us the truth.

168
00:11:27,486 --> 00:11:28,854
Will there be a rematch?

169
00:11:30,256 --> 00:11:33,259
Naturally. The game wasn't over yet.

170
00:11:33,426 --> 00:11:35,828
A word to your fans, please.

171
00:11:39,265 --> 00:11:40,566
Mr. Gotanda!

172
00:11:42,902 --> 00:11:44,470
Are you okay?

173
00:11:44,770 --> 00:11:45,871
Someone, help!

174
00:11:50,476 --> 00:11:52,845
Move...

175
00:11:53,646 --> 00:11:54,513
You okay?

176
00:11:55,614 --> 00:11:56,916
I can't move my leg.

177
00:11:57,183 --> 00:11:58,150
Your leg now?

178
00:11:59,885 --> 00:12:01,520
Keep them upright.

179
00:12:03,122 --> 00:12:03,956
Try again.

180
00:12:05,458 --> 00:12:06,559
Get a stretcher!

181
00:12:06,926 --> 00:12:07,827
Now your arms.

182
00:12:22,041 --> 00:12:23,876
Is Dr. Morimoto on leave?

183
00:12:25,344 --> 00:12:26,679
To mend his broken heart.

184
00:12:26,946 --> 00:12:28,814
Oh…The marriage fraud.

185
00:12:29,281 --> 00:12:31,083
It totally crushed him.

186
00:12:33,519 --> 00:12:35,721
Let us begin the
emergency conference.

187
00:12:36,155 --> 00:12:38,924
Goro Gotanda, age 22, male.

188
00:12:39,125 --> 00:12:43,662
As you know, a Shogi prodigy
leading the game into the future.

189
00:12:45,931 --> 00:12:49,368
Yesterday during his match
against Shogi robot Mongoose

190
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:53,706
his right hand went into spasm
and he lost consciousness.

191
00:12:54,707 --> 00:12:59,945
He was transported here, regained
consciousness, and stabilized.

192
00:13:00,846 --> 00:13:03,449
His cranial CT scan.

193
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:07,753
Multiple lesions and edema
in the left frontal lobe.

194
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:11,891
The CECT shows 1-cm to 2-cm
ring-enhancing lesions.

195
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:15,361
Blood tests were normal.

196
00:13:16,929 --> 00:13:18,364
This morning,

197
00:13:18,764 --> 00:13:20,299
loss of his right leg's motor control.

198
00:13:22,268 --> 00:13:28,274
But he regained it immediately and
test results were again normal.

199
00:13:30,743 --> 00:13:34,680
What is your diagnosis based
on these observations?

200
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,315
Dr. Ebina?

201
00:13:39,752 --> 00:13:42,021
Primary brain tumors.

202
00:13:42,154 --> 00:13:44,557
They could be metastatic.

203
00:13:44,723 --> 00:13:45,858
Yes. That's it.

204
00:13:47,993 --> 00:13:49,762
This is my diagnosis.

205
00:13:57,603 --> 00:14:01,173
73% brain abscess.
15% metastatic tumor.

206
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:04,076
7% gliomatosis.
5% others.

207
00:14:05,711 --> 00:14:09,281
Based on these figures,
my conclusion is brain abscess.

208
00:14:12,418 --> 00:14:14,486
How did you make this analysis?

209
00:14:15,521 --> 00:14:19,859
I used Hippocrates for this diagnosis.

210
00:14:21,493 --> 00:14:22,761
He used it.

211
00:14:24,096 --> 00:14:26,866
Hippocrates? What's that?

212
00:14:26,999 --> 00:14:28,200
Wait a minute.

213
00:14:29,134 --> 00:14:32,972
You were clear about
your skepticism of AI.

214
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:37,843
Dr. Ebina, keep talking like that
and you'll lose your job.

215
00:14:38,978 --> 00:14:41,747
AI can complete
10 years of research...

216
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:42,815
In one second.

217
00:14:43,115 --> 00:14:43,949
That's right.

218
00:14:46,652 --> 00:14:51,156
A brain abscess is a collection
of pus caused by bacterial infection.

219
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:52,958
The patient's MRI.

220
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:59,899
No abnormalities were confirmed
even in a full-body scan.

221
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:03,202
It's highly unlikely that
they're metastatic tumors.

222
00:15:03,802 --> 00:15:06,705
The symptoms on the right side
of his body were

223
00:15:07,172 --> 00:15:08,774
caused by the abscesses.

224
00:15:09,041 --> 00:15:12,478
They will all be removed
through surgery.

225
00:15:13,445 --> 00:15:16,015
The definitive treatment
advised by Hippocrates is

226
00:15:17,349 --> 00:15:19,118
brain abscess removal surgery.

227
00:15:22,288 --> 00:15:23,188
I object.

228
00:15:25,124 --> 00:15:26,592
To what? I'm listening.

229
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:28,861
He's listening.
Give it to him.

230
00:15:29,828 --> 00:15:31,664
Dr. Daimon, your diagnosis?

231
00:15:36,869 --> 00:15:37,703
Something's not right.

232
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:41,473
- Something?
- What's "something"?

233
00:15:41,974 --> 00:15:44,176
Don't object if you're not sure.

234
00:15:46,011 --> 00:15:47,947
I'm sure about one thing.

235
00:15:48,647 --> 00:15:49,648
Which is?

236
00:15:50,049 --> 00:15:51,216
This operation will

237
00:15:52,351 --> 00:15:53,552
fail with your skills.

238
00:16:00,159 --> 00:16:01,193
Get out.

239
00:16:02,561 --> 00:16:03,395
Yes sir.

240
00:16:07,533 --> 00:16:08,634
I don't believe it.

241
00:16:08,867 --> 00:16:11,503
Dr. Torii made Dr. Daimon obey him.

242
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:15,040
Dr. Morimoto, I have a bad feeling.

243
00:16:15,741 --> 00:16:19,011
I have the shivers...

244
00:16:23,082 --> 00:16:24,850
What's not right?

245
00:16:30,689 --> 00:16:31,991
Hello.

246
00:16:32,725 --> 00:16:34,927
Hey, can I run more tests...

247
00:16:41,533 --> 00:16:42,935
What happened?

248
00:16:50,943 --> 00:16:51,910
What happened?

249
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:04,523
Are you okay?

250
00:17:09,261 --> 00:17:10,996
What happened to me?

251
00:17:11,830 --> 00:17:12,998
You don't remember?

252
00:17:13,932 --> 00:17:14,933
No.

253
00:17:15,567 --> 00:17:17,036
Do you know where we are?

254
00:17:18,137 --> 00:17:19,938
Totei University Hospital.

255
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:21,340
Today's date?

256
00:17:22,641 --> 00:17:23,976
Transient impaired consciousness?

257
00:17:24,276 --> 00:17:26,712
Yeah. Temporary memory loss.

258
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:29,081
His brain is affected by pus?

259
00:17:30,182 --> 00:17:31,016
Possibly.

260
00:17:31,183 --> 00:17:33,685
The AI's answer was brain abscess.

261
00:17:34,153 --> 00:17:37,056
It's not to be taken lightly.

262
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:38,824
I guess not.

263
00:17:38,924 --> 00:17:42,094
Such a difficult diagnosis
in a blink of an eye...

264
00:17:42,261 --> 00:17:45,297
Maybe it means
humans can't beat AI.

265
00:17:45,731 --> 00:17:49,334
The human brain deteriorates
but machines don't age.

266
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:52,871
They can even be upgraded.
Reverse aging.

267
00:17:53,238 --> 00:17:55,074
The gap widens.

268
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:58,310
I wish humans can also be upgraded.

269
00:17:58,377 --> 00:17:59,211
Yeah.

270
00:17:59,278 --> 00:18:04,516
In any case, the hospital will
definitely concur with the AI.

271
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:06,952
It's the Totei AI Campaign.

272
00:18:09,555 --> 00:18:12,357
Maybe it's right...
Brain abscess.

273
00:18:12,491 --> 00:18:16,128
Do your wild instincts say otherwise?

274
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:21,767
Your wild instincts are wrong.

275
00:18:22,534 --> 00:18:23,402
That's the one.

276
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:26,839
A "baiman"
hand.

277
00:18:26,972 --> 00:18:28,273
Very big.

278
00:18:28,407 --> 00:18:32,344
Oh no…I shouldn't have
made this "pon" meld.

279
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:48,060
Look at all this badass data
from Hippocrates.

280
00:18:48,427 --> 00:18:50,963
It even includes the procedure
step by step.

281
00:18:52,164 --> 00:18:54,666
Follow this manual and
you can't go wrong.

282
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:58,370
Operations are done by humans.

283
00:19:03,075 --> 00:19:04,676
Did I say something to offend him?

284
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:18,757
Brain surgery?

285
00:19:19,291 --> 00:19:20,392
Don't worry.

286
00:19:20,759 --> 00:19:24,463
Hippocrates is going to
guide the procedure.

287
00:19:25,564 --> 00:19:26,899
Hippocrates again?

288
00:19:27,199 --> 00:19:31,637
You can trust the world's
most advanced AI.

289
00:19:34,873 --> 00:19:35,807
Mr. Gotanda...

290
00:19:37,442 --> 00:19:41,313
Please sign the consent form
for the operation.

291
00:19:44,449 --> 00:19:46,218
Three, six, gold.

292
00:19:46,285 --> 00:19:48,353
He said three, six, gold.

293
00:19:50,155 --> 00:19:51,023
Check.

294
00:19:51,089 --> 00:19:52,157
He said "check".

295
00:19:52,291 --> 00:19:55,394
I know. Stop pointing at me.

296
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:58,964
- Check.
- I told you to stop pointing.

297
00:19:59,064 --> 00:20:00,499
Read between the lines.

298
00:20:05,938 --> 00:20:06,772
I lose.

299
00:20:08,941 --> 00:20:10,275
Yes. I won.

300
00:20:10,475 --> 00:20:11,677
So childish.

301
00:20:11,910 --> 00:20:13,478
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

302
00:20:15,781 --> 00:20:18,350
Here's Mr. Gotanda's
consent form.

303
00:20:18,417 --> 00:20:19,618
For the operation?

304
00:20:21,453 --> 00:20:22,921
CONSENT FORM

305
00:20:22,988 --> 00:20:24,456
Do I understand correctly?

306
00:20:25,457 --> 00:20:26,625
Dr. Takashi Torii.

307
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:31,196
Shogi genius Gotanda's operation...

308
00:20:31,930 --> 00:20:34,433
This is your signature on
the lead surgeon's line.

309
00:20:34,499 --> 00:20:37,669
Are you planning on it?

310
00:20:38,136 --> 00:20:40,572
Yes, I am.

311
00:20:40,706 --> 00:20:44,209
I'm unfamiliar with your
reputation as a surgeon.

312
00:20:46,011 --> 00:20:47,112
I'm...

313
00:20:47,813 --> 00:20:52,451
This operation will receive
a great deal of media exposure.

314
00:20:53,018 --> 00:20:55,587
Do you know what that means?

315
00:20:55,687 --> 00:21:00,926
The operation must be
flawless and brilliant.

316
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:02,594
Yes sir.

317
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:08,467
So who do you have in mind?

318
00:21:08,667 --> 00:21:11,637
I've already made the decision.

319
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,840
- Don't tell me...
- That's what I'm telling you.

320
00:21:15,874 --> 00:21:16,708
Excuse me.

321
00:21:16,842 --> 00:21:17,676
Yes?

322
00:21:19,978 --> 00:21:20,979
You wanted to see me?

323
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:22,180
Yes, I did.

324
00:21:22,748 --> 00:21:23,949
Dr. Michiko Daimon...

325
00:21:24,016 --> 00:21:29,488
I want you to operate on
Shogi genius Mr. Gotanda.

326
00:21:30,422 --> 00:21:31,390
I decline.

327
00:21:31,657 --> 00:21:33,091
You decline?

328
00:21:33,292 --> 00:21:36,428
Exactly why do you decline?

329
00:21:37,262 --> 00:21:39,665
We have no diagnosis yet.

330
00:21:39,998 --> 00:21:43,268
We can't operate without
further examination.

331
00:21:43,335 --> 00:21:45,904
The diagnosis is brain abscess.
Delivered by Hippocrates.

332
00:21:46,271 --> 00:21:47,606
No need to examine further.

333
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:50,876
So you're going to blindly
trust a machine?

334
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,111
And what's the cause?

335
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:55,147
What's your justification?

336
00:21:55,380 --> 00:21:57,182
It's...

337
00:21:57,516 --> 00:21:58,950
Don't underestimate operations.

338
00:22:03,422 --> 00:22:05,724
I never underestimate operations.

339
00:22:09,394 --> 00:22:11,129
I'm taking my lunch break.

340
00:22:11,430 --> 00:22:12,931
- Okay.
- Oh, lunch...

341
00:22:13,465 --> 00:22:14,399
We have a problem.

342
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:15,634
You're the problem.

343
00:22:16,134 --> 00:22:18,337
- Don't be such a wimp.
- I'm sorry.

344
00:22:18,470 --> 00:22:20,572
I should operate after all...

345
00:22:20,706 --> 00:22:22,140
That won't be necessary.

346
00:22:22,641 --> 00:22:23,608
No, Dr. Torii.

347
00:22:23,775 --> 00:22:27,179
I suppose I have no other choice.

348
00:22:27,479 --> 00:22:31,316
I'll have to pay the melon man
a rack or two.

349
00:22:31,983 --> 00:22:35,053
Money. It's always the answer.

350
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:53,004
Oh...

351
00:22:54,239 --> 00:22:56,475
I'm clueless about Shogi.

352
00:22:57,275 --> 00:22:59,478
This was my game against Mongoose.

353
00:22:59,811 --> 00:23:01,913
I was about to put the knight here.

354
00:23:02,681 --> 00:23:05,450
So that robot's called Mongoose.

355
00:23:06,685 --> 00:23:08,720
But if I had...

356
00:23:24,803 --> 00:23:25,937
I would have lost.

357
00:23:26,671 --> 00:23:29,808
Wow. You think that far ahead?

358
00:23:29,941 --> 00:23:31,176
Amazing.

359
00:23:31,343 --> 00:23:34,613
AI can analyze 5 million
moves per second.

360
00:23:35,247 --> 00:23:36,214
That many?

361
00:23:37,282 --> 00:23:40,051
The human brain is no match against it.

362
00:23:41,386 --> 00:23:45,056
One day,
AI may surpass human intelligence.

363
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,527
Me...

364
00:23:50,295 --> 00:23:51,396
Two things.

365
00:23:52,497 --> 00:23:53,331
What?

366
00:23:54,032 --> 00:23:55,600
Things I think about in a day.

367
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:58,236
Surgery and food.

368
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:00,839
Easy.

369
00:24:03,074 --> 00:24:06,678
Don't you get confused
when you think that far ahead?

370
00:24:08,146 --> 00:24:08,980
Sure.

371
00:24:11,149 --> 00:24:12,083
I do.

372
00:24:12,551 --> 00:24:13,718
What do you do then?

373
00:24:15,787 --> 00:24:17,622
I get confused
because I think too far ahead.

374
00:24:17,756 --> 00:24:18,890
When that happens,

375
00:24:19,891 --> 00:24:22,327
I eliminate the possibilities

376
00:24:23,295 --> 00:24:24,262
one by one.

377
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:25,964
Eliminate?

378
00:24:26,531 --> 00:24:27,365
Yes.

379
00:24:28,567 --> 00:24:30,902
I empty my mind once.

380
00:24:31,937 --> 00:24:35,173
Then surprisingly, intuition takes over.

381
00:24:35,373 --> 00:24:36,741
It sort of showers down on me.

382
00:24:37,409 --> 00:24:40,979
Yeah! I totally understand.

383
00:24:41,446 --> 00:24:42,948
Do you really?

384
00:24:43,081 --> 00:24:43,915
Yeah.

385
00:24:44,449 --> 00:24:47,853
Intuition honed by my experience
with countless surgeries.

386
00:24:48,520 --> 00:24:52,691
That gut feeling I get
when things seem impossible.

387
00:24:53,558 --> 00:24:54,926
It does feel like a shower.

388
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:56,528
I see.

389
00:24:59,431 --> 00:25:02,801
That's how I think humans can beat AI.

390
00:25:03,668 --> 00:25:05,604
AI has no intuition or gut feelings.

391
00:25:08,773 --> 00:25:10,175
I bet you can win.

392
00:25:11,109 --> 00:25:12,277
Maybe.

393
00:25:15,146 --> 00:25:16,882
Will you operate on me?

394
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:19,017
What?

395
00:25:20,285 --> 00:25:22,020
We'll make a good team.

396
00:25:45,143 --> 00:25:47,078
It's been a while, Mr. Kanbara.

397
00:25:47,379 --> 00:25:48,780
You chose a fabulous place.

398
00:25:48,847 --> 00:25:50,148
It fits the occasion.

399
00:25:51,182 --> 00:25:53,652
For a reunion of old friends.

400
00:25:55,554 --> 00:25:58,757
It's already been 45 years.

401
00:25:59,791 --> 00:26:02,761
I left Totei University Hospital.

402
00:26:03,228 --> 00:26:04,529
You stayed.

403
00:26:09,134 --> 00:26:10,035
Then...

404
00:26:11,036 --> 00:26:15,407
at the prime of my career as
the Japan Doctors Club chairman

405
00:26:15,807 --> 00:26:19,678
you reappeared in my life.

406
00:26:22,380 --> 00:26:24,349
Cut to the chase.

407
00:26:25,450 --> 00:26:27,152
Why did you want to see me?

408
00:26:28,620 --> 00:26:29,621
You haven't changed.

409
00:26:29,988 --> 00:26:31,256
As straightforward as ever.

410
00:26:32,557 --> 00:26:34,659
So I will cut to the chase.

411
00:26:36,328 --> 00:26:39,364
If every hospital in Japan
implements AI

412
00:26:40,398 --> 00:26:45,103
I imagine your wallet will
get considerably fatter.

413
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:48,206
To set the ball in motion

414
00:26:49,140 --> 00:26:51,910
you had Hippocrates
implemented in Totei

415
00:26:53,078 --> 00:26:55,947
the best medical institution
in the country.

416
00:26:56,214 --> 00:26:59,351
If Totei sets a fine example
in using AI,

417
00:26:59,551 --> 00:27:02,220
every affiliate hospital will follow suit.

418
00:27:03,922 --> 00:27:06,157
Is that your plan?

419
00:27:07,492 --> 00:27:11,596
Or has Director Hiruma
read between the lines?

420
00:27:12,497 --> 00:27:14,199
You also haven't changed.

421
00:27:14,366 --> 00:27:16,334
As perceptive as ever.

422
00:27:17,369 --> 00:27:21,406
That's why I couldn't survive
in an organization.

423
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:25,043
What do you want?

424
00:27:25,944 --> 00:27:27,345
What are you asking of me?

425
00:27:28,780 --> 00:27:29,614
Nothing.

426
00:27:31,516 --> 00:27:32,350
Just...

427
00:27:34,119 --> 00:27:39,791
don't take advantage of Michiko Daimon
to achieve your own goals.

428
00:27:41,493 --> 00:27:42,927
She's just a doctor

429
00:27:43,428 --> 00:27:45,997
who likes to perform surgeries.

430
00:27:46,398 --> 00:27:49,300
Even surgeries proposed by AI?

431
00:27:52,871 --> 00:27:54,739
She'll accept.

432
00:27:56,908 --> 00:27:59,878
She'll operate on anybody
under any situation.

433
00:28:00,945 --> 00:28:02,614
Because she's Doctor-X.

434
00:28:04,716 --> 00:28:05,650
Mr. Kanbara.

435
00:28:06,785 --> 00:28:09,921
Aren't you the one
who made her like that?

436
00:28:17,595 --> 00:28:18,530
Excuse me.

437
00:28:19,597 --> 00:28:20,532
Here you are.

438
00:28:29,441 --> 00:28:32,310
Enough of this boring subject.

439
00:28:33,311 --> 00:28:35,513
Right, Akky?

440
00:28:36,347 --> 00:28:40,318
The chairman of the Japan
Doctors Club serving me a drink...

441
00:28:40,885 --> 00:28:42,454
One of life's perks.

442
00:28:42,520 --> 00:28:43,388
Ucchy.

443
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:07,812
What's not right?

444
00:29:14,018 --> 00:29:15,987
- Does it hurt?
- Not really.

445
00:29:24,729 --> 00:29:25,897
What happened?

446
00:29:43,948 --> 00:29:44,849
No...

447
00:30:15,246 --> 00:30:16,681
WORLD OF SHOGI

448
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:19,617
SECRETES BEHIND GOTANDA'S STRENGTH

449
00:30:26,191 --> 00:30:28,393
GOTANDA'S LUCKY MEAL

450
00:30:32,697 --> 00:30:34,732
GRILLED PORK AND RICE

451
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:50,849
I thought I'd find you here.

452
00:30:52,150 --> 00:30:53,151
So you found me.

453
00:30:53,318 --> 00:30:55,119
You shouldn't sneak out
of the hospital.

454
00:30:56,354 --> 00:30:57,388
How did you know?

455
00:30:58,990 --> 00:31:01,960
This is the place
where you get your lucky meal.

456
00:31:02,460 --> 00:31:04,629
It triggered my winning streak.

457
00:31:04,729 --> 00:31:06,130
But you're not in a match.

458
00:31:07,031 --> 00:31:10,401
Yes, I am.
I'm right in the middle of one.

459
00:31:12,003 --> 00:31:13,605
My brain is getting cut open.

460
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:15,874
Let me eat my lucky meal.

461
00:31:21,112 --> 00:31:21,946
Fine.

462
00:31:23,448 --> 00:31:25,850
But let me see your arm first.

463
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:27,485
What?

464
00:31:30,255 --> 00:31:31,422
What happened here?

465
00:31:31,756 --> 00:31:32,790
I don't know.

466
00:31:34,192 --> 00:31:35,593
It was suddenly there one day.

467
00:31:36,728 --> 00:31:38,463
I had a bandage on it
during the match.

468
00:31:38,529 --> 00:31:39,297
Since when?

469
00:31:39,464 --> 00:31:40,598
About a month.

470
00:31:42,700 --> 00:31:43,635
Okay...

471
00:31:47,138 --> 00:31:50,074
Why don't you eat with me?

472
00:31:52,176 --> 00:31:54,112
Wait. It's not cooked.

473
00:31:54,178 --> 00:31:56,581
I like it really rare.

474
00:31:59,350 --> 00:32:01,452
- What is it?
- Were you overseas lately?

475
00:32:03,087 --> 00:32:06,424
Last year, to several countries
as the Shogi ambassador.

476
00:32:06,758 --> 00:32:08,893
Did you eat rare pork
during your trip?

477
00:32:09,394 --> 00:32:10,228
Yes.

478
00:32:10,561 --> 00:32:12,430
- Get up...
- Why?

479
00:32:16,067 --> 00:32:17,235
We have to go back.

480
00:32:17,302 --> 00:32:20,405
Wait…Hold on.

481
00:32:33,418 --> 00:32:35,787
It might not be brain abscess?

482
00:32:36,087 --> 00:32:37,021
I don't know yet.

483
00:32:48,599 --> 00:32:52,370
Hippocrates, a world-renowned
AI developed here in Japan

484
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:54,806
diagnosed Shogi genius Gotanda.

485
00:32:55,006 --> 00:32:58,543
I, Takashi Torii, will be
operating on him.

486
00:32:59,544 --> 00:33:00,511
What's the diagnosis?

487
00:33:01,612 --> 00:33:03,047
Right. The diagnosis.

488
00:33:03,414 --> 00:33:09,420
Mr. Gotanda has given us his consent
to disclose the information.

489
00:33:09,854 --> 00:33:13,391
The diagnosis is brain abscess.

490
00:33:13,691 --> 00:33:16,160
Brain abscess?

491
00:33:16,361 --> 00:33:19,964
This genius, the future
of the Shogi world

492
00:33:20,198 --> 00:33:24,569
will be saved by artificial intelligence

493
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:27,238
which is the future in medicine.

494
00:33:27,305 --> 00:33:30,508
Director Hiruma,
what exactly is a brain abscess?

495
00:33:30,575 --> 00:33:32,577
Can Dr. Torii handle the op?

496
00:33:33,344 --> 00:33:37,348
Even an intern can with
Hippocrates providing instructions.

497
00:33:38,616 --> 00:33:40,551
Normally the brain is...

498
00:33:40,651 --> 00:33:42,020
We're talking about Dr. Torii.

499
00:33:42,820 --> 00:33:43,955
Drop it.

500
00:33:49,394 --> 00:33:50,595
Director Hiruma...

501
00:33:54,332 --> 00:33:55,199
Oh...

502
00:33:55,266 --> 00:33:58,002
You ignore Hippocrates
and involve us.

503
00:33:58,269 --> 00:34:02,507
We end up with a losing ticket
because of you.

504
00:34:02,673 --> 00:34:05,143
The patient gets the winning ticket.

505
00:34:05,276 --> 00:34:09,213
He certainly won't if the wrong
procedure is performed on him.

506
00:34:09,580 --> 00:34:12,216
You're getting bold,
First Assistant.

507
00:34:14,752 --> 00:34:16,154
Stop this at once.

508
00:34:17,188 --> 00:34:19,157
Nice timing. Work the suction.

509
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:20,925
Hurry up.

510
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:23,327
Suction.

511
00:34:27,532 --> 00:34:28,399
Right here.

512
00:34:50,555 --> 00:34:51,522
There it is.

513
00:34:52,557 --> 00:34:53,391
There's what?

514
00:34:54,058 --> 00:34:54,892
A worm.

515
00:34:55,393 --> 00:34:56,227
Worm?

516
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:57,895
Pork bladder worm.

517
00:34:58,729 --> 00:34:59,764
It's a parasite.

518
00:34:59,831 --> 00:35:00,665
Yes.

519
00:35:07,905 --> 00:35:09,941
Dr. Daimon learned that

520
00:35:10,007 --> 00:35:13,377
the patient ate raw pork
while travelling abroad.

521
00:35:13,444 --> 00:35:15,980
So she ran some tests

522
00:35:16,114 --> 00:35:18,149
and found two tapeworm larvae

523
00:35:18,282 --> 00:35:20,818
or bladder worms,
in his arm and back.

524
00:35:27,158 --> 00:35:30,094
That's how she knew it was cysticercosis?

525
00:35:30,161 --> 00:35:34,098
He ingested tapeworm larvae
from measly pork and

526
00:35:34,365 --> 00:35:36,701
the oncospheres hatched
inside his body.

527
00:35:36,934 --> 00:35:41,806
Then the cysticerci localized in
his brain and caused the symptoms.

528
00:35:42,073 --> 00:35:43,274
Impossible.

529
00:35:43,574 --> 00:35:46,210
Hippocrates's diagnosis was brain abscess.

530
00:35:47,979 --> 00:35:49,914
I also never fail a diagnosis.

531
00:35:54,252 --> 00:35:55,753
There's another one.

532
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:57,822
Removing cyst.

533
00:35:58,389 --> 00:36:00,091
I'll pull this way.

534
00:36:00,591 --> 00:36:01,792
Elevator.

535
00:36:30,855 --> 00:36:32,957
All bladder worms
have been removed.

536
00:36:40,364 --> 00:36:41,265
We're done.

537
00:36:41,332 --> 00:36:45,036
BP 115 over 72.
Pulse 63, normal sinus rhythm.

538
00:36:51,676 --> 00:36:52,877
We won this match.

539
00:36:54,345 --> 00:36:56,013
- Good job.
- Good job.

540
00:36:56,080 --> 00:36:57,014
Good job.

541
00:37:22,473 --> 00:37:23,608
Daimon!

542
00:37:24,909 --> 00:37:29,247
How did you diagnose a condition
that eluded both the AI and me?

543
00:37:30,348 --> 00:37:32,383
Because AI doesn't eat.

544
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:33,584
Huh?

545
00:37:36,854 --> 00:37:38,856
And you need to study more.

546
00:37:39,857 --> 00:37:41,192
I need to study more?

547
00:37:42,994 --> 00:37:46,130
I've written hundreds of
more articles than you.

548
00:37:51,502 --> 00:37:55,306
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

549
00:38:00,044 --> 00:38:05,316
Thank you for employing Daimon
and Jonouchi from our agency.

550
00:38:07,184 --> 00:38:08,252
Melon.

551
00:38:10,321 --> 00:38:11,722
The bill.

552
00:38:16,160 --> 00:38:19,130
Daimon performed the operation
without permission.

553
00:38:20,598 --> 00:38:24,335
I refuse to pay a single penny
for this one.

554
00:38:25,136 --> 00:38:30,841
What's worse, Daimon desecrated
the diagnosis presented by AI.

555
00:38:31,475 --> 00:38:34,378
I should sue you for damages.

556
00:38:36,347 --> 00:38:37,515
Is that so?

557
00:38:37,581 --> 00:38:38,582
What?

558
00:38:38,749 --> 00:38:41,719
If Daimon didn't make
the correct diagnosis

559
00:38:42,320 --> 00:38:46,457
an inappropriate procedure would
have been conducted on the patient.

560
00:38:47,124 --> 00:38:50,561
Imagine what would've happened.

561
00:38:50,628 --> 00:38:56,267
And the patient is a famous
Shogi genius, Goro Gotanda.

562
00:38:57,201 --> 00:39:00,171
It would've created a media frenzy.

563
00:39:01,172 --> 00:39:07,144
Totei University Hospital would have
no doubt lost public confidence.

564
00:39:18,422 --> 00:39:20,358
$10,000,000

565
00:39:22,493 --> 00:39:25,896
Scraping off one or two zeros...

566
00:39:26,530 --> 00:39:28,699
Is that one of your services?

567
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:30,201
No.

568
00:39:30,935 --> 00:39:33,204
If we keep our mouths shut

569
00:39:33,771 --> 00:39:35,873
the sales of Hippocrates
will skyrocket.

570
00:39:36,374 --> 00:39:40,044
You and Chairman Uchikanda
will skyrocket to cloud nine.

571
00:39:40,911 --> 00:39:44,849
Even with one or two more zeros

572
00:39:45,216 --> 00:39:48,953
I believe it's an incredible bargain.

573
00:39:51,555 --> 00:39:54,725
Please don't add more zeros.

574
00:39:55,593 --> 00:39:56,594
Yes sir.

575
00:39:58,195 --> 00:40:01,532
Thank you, Ucchy!

576
00:40:01,632 --> 00:40:02,633
Ole!

577
00:40:06,704 --> 00:40:09,440
Thank you!

578
00:40:10,341 --> 00:40:12,510
REMATCH

579
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:20,317
Gotanda, a Shogi genius
in a realm of the divine.

580
00:40:20,618 --> 00:40:23,954
And Mongoose, the world's
strongest Shogi robot.

581
00:40:31,162 --> 00:40:35,232
Their rematch has now begun.

582
00:40:37,568 --> 00:40:41,272
Which will prevail?
Human or artificial intelligence?

583
00:40:41,605 --> 00:40:43,274
Let's keep watching.

584
00:40:52,850 --> 00:40:54,685
Dr. Daimon, it's time.

585
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:56,987
Okay.

586
00:41:07,865 --> 00:41:09,633
As you see here

587
00:41:09,767 --> 00:41:13,804
Mr. Gotanda has made
a perfect recovery.

588
00:41:13,971 --> 00:41:17,675
Just as AI Hippocrates diagnosed...

589
00:41:18,242 --> 00:41:19,076
Brain abscess.

590
00:41:19,743 --> 00:41:23,881
They were impeccably removed by Dr. Torii.

591
00:41:24,381 --> 00:41:26,383
Artificial intelligence and

592
00:41:26,450 --> 00:41:30,788
Totei University Hospital's
intelligence and skills

593
00:41:30,988 --> 00:41:34,725
saved the Shogi wonder's life.

594
00:41:35,059 --> 00:41:39,296
How about a big applause
for Dr. Torii?

595
00:41:47,972 --> 00:41:48,806
No.

596
00:41:50,574 --> 00:41:53,444
There's something I must tell you.

597
00:41:53,511 --> 00:41:56,747
It wasn't brain abscess.
It was cysticercosis.

598
00:41:56,881 --> 00:41:58,415
- Stop it.
- I'm sorry.

599
00:41:58,582 --> 00:41:59,450
He said it.

600
00:41:59,650 --> 00:42:00,751
Torii's revolt.

601
00:42:02,486 --> 00:42:03,921
Cysticercosis is...

602
00:42:03,988 --> 00:42:05,789
Dr. Torii, that's enough.

603
00:42:05,856 --> 00:42:07,958
They were worms.
I can't deny that.

604
00:42:08,025 --> 00:42:08,959
Dr. Torii!

605
00:42:09,727 --> 00:42:11,929
- Ebina! Hara.
- Yes sir...

606
00:42:12,897 --> 00:42:15,533
Dr. Torii, come with me.

607
00:42:15,599 --> 00:42:16,534
Let go of me.

608
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:19,403
Shut the hell up.

609
00:42:19,470 --> 00:42:20,371
Dr. Ebina, your language.

610
00:42:20,437 --> 00:42:22,072
He had worms!

611
00:42:24,642 --> 00:42:25,743
What was that about?

612
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,345
Director Hiruma, worms?

613
00:42:28,579 --> 00:42:30,414
You tell me.

614
00:42:30,481 --> 00:42:33,350
- Hippocrates made a misdiagnosis?
- Absolutely not.

615
00:42:33,417 --> 00:42:35,719
- Director Hiruma...
- Come on...

616
00:42:35,786 --> 00:42:37,788
Calm down. Please.

617
00:42:38,656 --> 00:42:39,590
Listen.

618
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:46,630
The patient had brain abscess,
just as Hippocrates diagnosed.

619
00:42:47,331 --> 00:42:48,666
In 2017

620
00:42:49,166 --> 00:42:54,438
the university medical system
regained its once-lost authority

621
00:42:55,072 --> 00:43:01,078
and the system on which lives depend
strayed away from what it should be.

622
00:43:03,147 --> 00:43:04,381
They were worms...

623
00:43:24,168 --> 00:43:25,302
I'm back.

624
00:43:27,504 --> 00:43:28,539
Who's winning?

625
00:43:29,006 --> 00:43:30,774
The robot, unmistakably.

626
00:43:31,175 --> 00:43:33,243
Mr. Gotanda is getting cornered.

627
00:43:33,711 --> 00:43:35,212
Oh yeah?

628
00:43:36,046 --> 00:43:40,718
<i>In the midst of all this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

629
00:43:41,385 --> 00:43:45,556
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

630
00:43:47,658 --> 00:43:49,693
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

631
00:43:50,728 --> 00:43:53,497
<i>Despising the herd</i>
<i>mentality, authority</i>

632
00:43:53,564 --> 00:43:54,999
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

633
00:43:55,566 --> 00:44:00,771
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

634
00:44:16,520 --> 00:44:19,189
Gotanda just played
his ace in the hole.

635
00:44:19,556 --> 00:44:21,158
The"Knight" from "Hell" maneuver.

636
00:44:25,929 --> 00:44:29,433
Michiko, there could be a miracle.

637
00:44:29,566 --> 00:44:31,368
That move turned the tide.

638
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:32,403
Really?

639
00:44:37,574 --> 00:44:39,743
He emptied his mind.

640
00:45:05,302 --> 00:45:06,403
He won!

641
00:45:06,470 --> 00:45:09,606
Gotanda wins with 162 moves!

642
00:45:11,008 --> 00:45:12,342
He won!

643
00:45:12,409 --> 00:45:13,577
Yes!

644
00:45:16,980 --> 00:45:18,615
Let's go celebrate!

645
00:45:19,183 --> 00:45:21,952
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

646
00:45:22,553 --> 00:45:23,587
<i>Also known as...</i>

647
00:45:24,288 --> 00:45:25,923
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

648
00:45:26,256 --> 00:45:28,859
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

649
00:45:29,426 --> 00:45:30,561
Are you really a doctor?

650
00:45:30,627 --> 00:45:32,262
If you were a patient,
you'd understand.

651
00:45:32,329 --> 00:45:33,597
I had enough.

652
00:45:33,664 --> 00:45:36,533
- Am I going to die?
- I'm sorry for the couple.

653
00:45:36,600 --> 00:45:37,568
Simultaneous surgery.

654
00:45:37,634 --> 00:45:39,069
This procedure is impossible.

655
00:45:39,136 --> 00:45:40,104
Change surgeon.

656
00:45:40,237 --> 00:45:43,674
If the anesthesiologist is here,
I won't do surgery.
